# Live capture: MVS 3.8j TK5 (Update 5) under Hercules, recorded 2026-08-17.
#
# Host: localhost:3271 (TK5's CNSLPORT set by hand; VM/370 holds 3270 on this box).
# Script: connect, RESET+CLEAR to dismiss the logo, then "TSO" at VTAM's USS panel.
# 16 commands, 0 errors, 0 program checks.
#
# WHAT THIS IS AND IS NOT. This is a PRE-LOGON capture. It covers real MVS traffic:
# the Hercules connection banner, VTAM's USS logon panel (the TK5 logo with its
# single unprotected field at SBA(1770) carrying IC), and VTAM rejecting an
# unrecognized token with IKT00405I. It does NOT reach TSO.
#
# TSO on this system rejects the terminal type we advertise, IBM-3278-2. This is NOT
# a TN3270E problem: measured with s3270 against this host, with the TN3270E telnet
# option (40) never negotiated in any run, IBM-3278-2 fails with IKT00405I while
# IBM-3278-2-E, IBM-3279-2-E and IBM-DYNAMIC all reach TSO. The -E suffix means
# extended data stream in the ttype string, which is a different thing from the
# TN3270E option. Our inbound records are byte-identical to s3270's successful ones,
# so the gap is one string. See docs/live-testing.md for the full comparison, and
# for the earlier wrong diagnosis that blamed TN3270E.
#
# NO CREDENTIALS ARE PRESENT. Nothing secret was typed: the only input is the
# literal string "TSO" and a Clear. Verified zero occurrences of any TK5 password's
# EBCDIC bytes. A future TSO capture WILL contain a password and must be redacted.
#
# Useful properties for testing: an all-protected screen (25 SF(0x60) + 8 SF(0xe8),
# no IC) followed by a formatted panel with exactly one unprotected field, plus a
# host that replaces the whole screen via EraseWrite rather than updating in place.
